Z||000004||Bruce||08-10-2001||02:52 AM||||I have the same car (86 GT) and had the same problem. The shifter cables wear and the shifter doesn't move over far enough to engage the back-up lights on its own. Somewhere, in the forum archives, is an exact explanation of the adjustment process.<BR>Hope this helps.<BR>b||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||08-10-2001||07:57 AM||||My 85SE v-6 4speed does the same thing.<P>In my case it has nothing to do with the switch.  There is a cam sort of ramp that holds the shifter in the far left position when in reverse.  This holds the stick against the reverse switch.<P>The cam is worn and rarely holds the stick in the far left position.  If I hold it there myself the back-up lights work fine.<P>I think I can use my dremmel tool and grind a bit of slope back into the ramp to make it work but that's way down on my priority list.||||reg||1
